According to SourceForge the domain was renewed late last week and
they are in the process of re-setting the DNS info so the address
should be back up shortly.

I share your concerns about VA but, in this case, I think it's OK
to let SourceForge continue to host `linuxia64'.  Hopefully there's
not much they can do to screw up a DNS listing.

If we do decide to pull the site from SourceForge I think a better
solution would be to transfer the domain name rather than try and
start a new one.  If SF still give us problems, and an appropriate
entity is willing to provide hosting, I'm sure we can arrange to
transfer the domain.

